 The server inside keeps the modes of its chats and has no Settings of its own, so the host tells it the default from Settings → Sessions, `permissionDefaultMode` in the host's `settings.json`, the way it tells the idle stop: `space-permission-default.js` holds both sides. The host writes `{ mode }` into `$HOME/.openchamber-space/permission-default.json` over `exec`, through a temporary name, when a space is made, at every start and restart, and to every running space when the setting changes, from the settings runtime's `onPermissionDefaultModeChanged`. These writes take turns with the idle stop's, so a space started during a change gets the changed mode. A value that is no mode is written as `ask`. A write that fails is logged and the space keeps the mode it had.
 
