 The agent can rewrite the file and gains nothing by it: it runs as the same user as the server inside, which owns that server's settings and its token, so it can set any chat's mode without the file. Measured in a space: the agent's user can write `~/.config/openchamber/settings.json`, read the token and write the project's `opencode.json`. The mode protects the user from what the agent does inside the container, never anything from the agent.
 
